    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "05. Attack Sequence",
    "ruleNumber": "05.00",
    "order": 91,
    "anchor": "05.00",
    "summary": "The attack sequence settles whether attacks inflict damage. Whenever the [active player](vsdata:core-rule/active-player-and-opposing-player) is told to resolve it, they take 4 steps in order, rolling all the dice a step needs at once:\n\n1. **[Hit Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls)** (05.01)\n2. **[Wound Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls)** (05.02)\n3. **[Save Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/save-rolls)** (05.03)\n4. [Inflict Damage](vsdata:core-rule/inflict-damage) (05.04)\n\nAn attack leaves the sequence once it fails or inflicts damage; when every attack has done one or the other, they are resolved.\n\nA **critical hit** is still a hit and a **critical wound** still a wound, and either can trigger rules such as **[[LETHAL HITS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/lethal-hits)** and **[[DEVASTATING WOUNDS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/devastating-wounds)**.",
